<div id="fern-app">

  <div class="fern-card">
    <h4>1. Start simple: one point, one rule</h4>
    <p class="fern-desc">A <strong>rule</strong> takes a point (x, y) and maps it to a new point
      (x&prime;, y&prime;) = (a&middot;x + b&middot;y + e, c&middot;x + d&middot;y + f).
      That's it -- six numbers, one point in, one point out. Try the sliders, then press
      "Apply this rule again" to feed the new point back into the same rule, and watch where it goes next.</p>
    <div class="fern-row">
      <div class="fern-sidebar">
        <h6>Starting point</h6>
        <label for="fern-s1-x0">x</label>
        <input id="fern-s1-x0" type="number" step="0.1" value="1.0">
        <label for="fern-s1-y0">y</label>
        <input id="fern-s1-y0" type="number" step="0.1" value="1.0">
        <h6 style="margin-top:10px;">The rule</h6>
        <label for="fern-s1-a">a: <strong id="fern-s1-a-val">0.70</strong></label>
        <input id="fern-s1-a" type="range" min="-1.5" max="1.5" step="0.05" value="0.70">
        <label for="fern-s1-b">b: <strong id="fern-s1-b-val">-0.50</strong></label>
        <input id="fern-s1-b" type="range" min="-1.5" max="1.5" step="0.05" value="-0.50">
        <label for="fern-s1-c">c: <strong id="fern-s1-c-val">0.50</strong></label>
        <input id="fern-s1-c" type="range" min="-1.5" max="1.5" step="0.05" value="0.50">
        <label for="fern-s1-d">d: <strong id="fern-s1-d-val">0.70</strong></label>
        <input id="fern-s1-d" type="range" min="-1.5" max="1.5" step="0.05" value="0.70">
        <label for="fern-s1-e">e: <strong id="fern-s1-e-val">0.40</strong></label>
        <input id="fern-s1-e" type="range" min="-2.0" max="2.0" step="0.1" value="0.40">
        <label for="fern-s1-f">f: <strong id="fern-s1-f-val">0.20</strong></label>
        <input id="fern-s1-f" type="range" min="-2.0" max="2.0" step="0.1" value="0.20">
        <div class="fern-btn-row">
          <button id="fern-s1-apply" class="fern-btn-primary" type="button">Apply this rule again</button>
          <button id="fern-s1-reset" class="fern-btn-secondary" type="button">Reset</button>
        </div>
        <div id="fern-s1-summary" class="fern-summary"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fern-canvas-wrap">
        <canvas id="fern-canvas-1" width="480" height="420"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="fern-card">
    <h4>2. Add more rules -- and randomness</h4>
    <p class="fern-desc">Fractals don't use one fixed rule -- they repeat a simple recipe, over and over:
      start at any point; pick one of the triangle's three corners at random, each equally likely;
      move the current point exactly halfway towards that corner, and plot the new point; then repeat,
      tens of thousands of times. Do that, and out comes the famous <strong>Sierpinski triangle</strong>.
      (This "halfway to a random corner" trick is special to the triangle -- try it on a square and you
      just get a solidly filled square, not a fractal. The fern below gets its fractal structure a
      different way, using rules that rotate and stretch as well as shrink.)</p>
    <div class="fern-row">
      <div class="fern-sidebar">
        <h6>Number of points</h6>
        <input id="fern-s2-n" type="range" min="500" max="8000" step="500" value="4000">
        <div class="fern-btn-row">
          <button id="fern-s2-animate" class="fern-btn-primary" type="button">Watch it build, point by point</button>
        </div>
        <div id="fern-s2-summary" class="fern-summary"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fern-canvas-wrap">
        <canvas id="fern-canvas-2" width="480" height="420"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="fern-card">
    <h4>3. Barnsley's fern, simplified</h4>
    <p class="fern-desc">Same idea again -- several rules, chosen at random, applied over and over -- but
      now with Barnsley's own four published rules for a fern. All 28 of the raw numbers behind those
      four rules matter, but that's too many to play with directly, so here are four knobs that each
      nudge a meaningful part of the shape. All four start at the setting that reproduces Barnsley's
      exact original fern; most other settings look nothing like a fern, and a few don't converge at all.</p>
    <div class="fern-row">
      <div class="fern-sidebar">
        <h6>Number of points</h6>
        <input id="fern-s3-n" type="range" min="1000" max="40000" step="1000" value="15000">
        <div class="fern-btn-row">
          <button id="fern-s3-animate" class="fern-btn-primary" type="button">Watch it build, point by point</button>
        </div>
        <hr>
        <h6>Colour</h6>
        <div class="fern-radio">
          <label><input type="radio" name="fern-s3-color" value="natural" checked> Natural green</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="fern-s3-color" value="rule"> By generating rule (see the self-similarity)</label>
        </div>
        <hr>
        <h6>Shape</h6>
        <label for="fern-s3-rotation">Leaflet rotation: <strong id="fern-s3-rotation-val">0</strong>&deg;</label>
        <input id="fern-s3-rotation" type="range" min="-45" max="45" step="1" value="0">
        <label for="fern-s3-leaflet">Leaflet size: <strong id="fern-s3-leaflet-val">1.0</strong></label>
        <input id="fern-s3-leaflet" type="range" min="0.2" max="7.0" step="0.1" value="1.0">
        <label for="fern-s3-stem">Stem length: <strong id="fern-s3-stem-val">1.0</strong></label>
        <input id="fern-s3-stem" type="range" min="0.2" max="5.0" step="0.1" value="1.0">
        <label for="fern-s3-lean">Overall lean: <strong id="fern-s3-lean-val">0.0</strong></label>
        <input id="fern-s3-lean" type="range" min="-4.0" max="4.0" step="0.1" value="0.0">
        <div class="fern-btn-row">
          <button id="fern-s3-reset" class="fern-btn-secondary" type="button">Reset to Barnsley's fern</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fern-canvas-wrap">
        <canvas id="fern-canvas" width="640" height="700"></canvas>
        <div id="fern-s3-summary" class="fern-summary"></div>
        <details class="fern-rules-table">
          <summary>See the raw numbers these four knobs produce</summary>
          <ul id="fern-s3-rules-list"></ul>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<script>
(function () {
  "use strict";
  if (window.SHOW_JS_APPS === false) return;

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Ported 1:1 (same maths, same constants) from the Python/Shinylive
  // version (fractal_app/app.py). Runs as plain JavaScript, entirely in
  // the browser -- no Python runtime to download.
  //
  // Each "rule" is an affine map (x,y) -> (a*x+b*y+e, c*x+d*y+f). The
  // "chaos game" repeatedly picks one of several rules at random (each
  // with a fixed probability) and applies it to wherever the last point
  // landed -- that's the entire mechanism behind every panel below.
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------

  var root = document.getElementById("fern-app");
  if (!root) return;

  var SEED = 42;
  var CLIP = 1.0e4;

  function $(id) { return root.querySelector("#" + id); }

  function fmtN(n) {
    n = Math.round(n);
    var s = String(n);
    var out = "";
    var c = 0;
    for (var i = s.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
      out = s[i] + out;
      c++;
      if (c % 3 === 0 && i !== 0) out = "," + out;
    }
    return out;
  }

  // A tiny deterministic PRNG (mulberry32). Re-seeding with the same
  // SEED and drawing n numbers always gives the same first n draws as
  // drawing 2n numbers would -- that's what guarantees that the first
  // N points of a run are always exactly a prefix of a bigger run with
  // the same rules, letting "Watch it build" reveal a real, continuing
  // construction rather than a new random one each frame.
  function makeRng(seed) {
    var s = seed >>> 0;
    return function () {
      s |= 0;
      s = (s + 0x6D2B79F5) | 0;
      var t = Math.imul(s ^ (s >>> 15), 1 | s);
      t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;
      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;
    };
  }

  function clipPoint(x, y) {
    var clipped = false;
    if (!isFinite(x)) { x = 0.0; clipped = true; }
    else if (Math.abs(x) > CLIP) { x = CLIP * (x < 0 ? -1 : 1); clipped = true; }
    if (!isFinite(y)) { y = 0.0; clipped = true; }
    else if (Math.abs(y) > CLIP) { y = CLIP * (y < 0 ? -1 : 1); clipped = true; }
    return [x, y, clipped];
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Section 1: a single point, mapped by a single rule, repeatedly.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  function iterateSingleRule(x0, y0, a, b, c, d, e, f, n) {
    var xs = [x0], ys = [y0];
    var clipped = false;
    var x = x0, y = y0;
    for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      var nx = a * x + b * y + e;
      var ny = c * x + d * y + f;
      var r = clipPoint(nx, ny);
      nx = r[0]; ny = r[1]; clipped = clipped || r[2];
      xs.push(nx); ys.push(ny);
      x = nx; y = ny;
    }
    return { xs: xs, ys: ys, clipped: clipped };
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Shared "chaos game" mechanism for sections 2 and 3.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  function normalizeProbs(rules) {
    var n = rules.length;
    var raw = rules.map(function (r) { return Math.max(r[6], 0.0); });
    var total = raw.reduce(function (a, b) { return a + b; }, 0);
    if (total <= 0) return rules.map(function () { return 1.0 / n; });
    return raw.map(function (p) { return p / total; });
  }

  function generatePoints(nPoints, rules, seed) {
    var probs = normalizeProbs(rules);
    var cum = [];
    var acc = 0.0;
    for (var i = 0; i < probs.length; i++) { acc += probs[i]; cum.push(acc); }
    cum[cum.length - 1] = 1.0;

    var rng = makeRng(seed === undefined ? SEED : seed);
    var xs = new Array(nPoints);
    var ys = new Array(nPoints);
    var ruleIdx = new Array(nPoints);
    var x = 0.0, y = 0.0;
    var clipped = false;
    for (var n = 0; n < nPoints; n++) {
      var r = rng();
      var k = 0;
      while (r > cum[k]) k++;
      var rule = rules[k];
      var nx = rule[0] * x + rule[1] * y + rule[4];
      var ny = rule[2] * x + rule[3] * y + rule[5];
      var cp = clipPoint(nx, ny);
      nx = cp[0]; ny = cp[1]; clipped = clipped || cp[2];
      x = nx; y = ny;
      xs[n] = x; ys[n] = y; ruleIdx[n] = k;
    }
    return { xs: xs, ys: ys, ruleIdx: ruleIdx, clipped: clipped };
  }

  function dataBounds(xs, ys, from, to) {
    var xmin = Infinity, xmax = -Infinity, ymin = Infinity, ymax = -Infinity;
    for (var i = from; i < to; i++) {
      if (xs[i] < xmin) xmin = xs[i];
      if (xs[i] > xmax) xmax = xs[i];
      if (ys[i] < ymin) ymin = ys[i];
      if (ys[i] > ymax) ymax = ys[i];
    }
    if (!isFinite(xmin)) { xmin = -1; xmax = 1; ymin = -1; ymax = 1; }
    return [xmin, xmax, ymin, ymax];
  }

  function computeTransform(xmin, xmax, ymin, ymax, W, H) {
    var xpad = (xmax - xmin) * 0.06 + 0.05;
    var ypad = (ymax - ymin) * 0.06 + 0.05;
    xmin -= xpad; xmax += xpad; ymin -= ypad; ymax += ypad;
    var dataW = Math.max(xmax - xmin, 1e-6);
    var dataH = Math.max(ymax - ymin, 1e-6);
    var scale = Math.min(W / dataW, H / dataH);
    var offX = (W - dataW * scale) / 2;
    var offY = (H - dataH * scale) / 2;
    return {
      sx: function (x) { return offX + (x - xmin) * scale; },
      sy: function (y) { return H - (offY + (y - ymin) * scale); }
    };
  }

  // Draws points [0, n) from xs/ys onto ctx, optionally coloured by which
  // rule drew each one, optionally highlighting the most recent point.
  function drawPoints(ctx, W, H, xs, ys, ruleIdx, n, colorMode, colors, baseColor, highlightI) {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    ctx.fillStyle = "#fbfbf8";
    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
    if (n <= 0) return;
    var b = dataBounds(xs, ys, 0, n);
    var tr = computeTransform(b[0], b[1], b[2], b[3], W, H);
    var sz = 1.6;
    var half = sz / 2;

    if (colorMode === "rule") {
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.65;
      for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        ctx.fillStyle = colors[ruleIdx[i]];
        var px = tr.sx(xs[i]), py = tr.sy(ys[i]);
        ctx.fillRect(px - half, py - half, sz, sz);
      }
    } else {
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.55;
      ctx.fillStyle = baseColor;
      for (var j = 0; j < n; j++) {
        var qx = tr.sx(xs[j]), qy = tr.sy(ys[j]);
        ctx.fillRect(qx - half, qy - half, sz, sz);
      }
    }
    ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;

    if (highlightI !== undefined && highlightI !== null && highlightI >= 0 && highlightI < n) {
      var hx = tr.sx(xs[highlightI]), hy = tr.sy(ys[highlightI]);
      if (highlightI > 0) {
        var px2 = tr.sx(xs[highlightI - 1]), py2 = tr.sy(ys[highlightI - 1]);
        ctx.strokeStyle = "#d81b60";
        ctx.lineWidth = 1.0;
        ctx.globalAlpha = 0.85;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(px2, py2);
        ctx.lineTo(hx, hy);
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;
      }
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.fillStyle = "#d81b60";
      ctx.arc(hx, hy, 5, 0, 2 * Math.PI);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.strokeStyle = "#fff";
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;
      ctx.stroke();
    }
  }

  function stepFormulaHtml(n, target, rules, ruleIdx, xs, ys, names, probs) {
    var k = ruleIdx[n - 1];
    var r = rules[k];
    var a = r[0], b = r[1], c = r[2], d = r[3], e = r[4], f = r[5];
    var px = n >= 2 ? xs[n - 2] : 0.0, py = n >= 2 ? ys[n - 2] : 0.0;
    var nx = xs[n - 1], ny = ys[n - 1];
    var lines = [];
    lines.push("<strong>Step " + fmtN(n) + " of " + fmtN(target) + "</strong> -- this point was drawn by the " +
      "<strong>" + names[k] + "</strong> rule (chosen with probability " + Math.round(probs[k] * 100) + "%):");
    lines.push(
      "x = " + a.toFixed(2) + " &times; " + px.toFixed(3) + " + " + b.toFixed(2) + " &times; " + py.toFixed(3) +
      " + " + e.toFixed(2) + " = <strong>" + nx.toFixed(3) + "</strong><br>" +
      "y = " + c.toFixed(2) + " &times; " + px.toFixed(3) + " + " + d.toFixed(2) + " &times; " + py.toFixed(3) +
      " + " + f.toFixed(2) + " = <strong>" + ny.toFixed(3) + "</strong>"
    );
    return lines.join("<br><br>");
  }

  // A "watch it build" controller: reveals `target` points one at a time
  // for the first `slowPoints`, with a short narrated formula each time,
  // then in a fixed number of fast batches for the rest -- exactly the
  // slow-then-fast pacing of the original app. The batch size in the fast
  // phase is fixed by the FIXED amount of work left (target - slowPoints)
  // divided across fastFrames ticks, so it always finishes in that many
  // ticks regardless of target size.
  function makeWatchBuilder(opts) {
    var slowPoints = opts.slowPoints, slowDelay = opts.slowDelay;
    var fastFrames = opts.fastFrames, fastDelay = opts.fastDelay;
    var onReveal = opts.onReveal; // (revealed, animating) -> void
    var targetFn = opts.targetFn;
    var timerId = null;
    var animating = false;
    var revealed = 0;

    function stop() {
      animating = false;
      if (timerId !== null) { clearTimeout(timerId); timerId = null; }
    }

    function tick() {
      if (!animating) return;
      var target = targetFn();
      var current = revealed;
      var delay, newN;
      if (current < Math.min(slowPoints, target)) {
        delay = slowDelay;
        newN = current + 1;
      } else {
        delay = fastDelay;
        var fastTotal = Math.max(target - slowPoints, 1);
        var step = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(fastTotal / fastFrames));
        newN = Math.min(current + step, target);
      }
      revealed = newN;
      onReveal(revealed, true);
      if (newN >= target) { animating = false; timerId = null; return; }
      timerId = setTimeout(tick, delay);
    }

    function start() {
      stop();
      revealed = 0;
      animating = true;
      timerId = setTimeout(tick, slowDelay);
    }

    // Fast, non-narrated rebuild used whenever a slider changes without
    // pressing "watch it build": grows to the target in batches of a
    // few thousand points per animation frame via requestAnimationFrame,
    // so a change never draws tens of thousands of points synchronously
    // in one go (which can jank a phone's browser).
    function fastRebuild(batchSize) {
      stop();
      var target = targetFn();
      revealed = 0;
      function frame() {
        revealed = Math.min(revealed + batchSize, target);
        onReveal(revealed, false);
        if (revealed < target) {
          timerId = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
        } else {
          timerId = null;
        }
      }
      timerId = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    function jumpTo(n) {
      stop();
      revealed = n;
      onReveal(revealed, false);
    }

    return {
      start: start, stop: stop, fastRebuild: fastRebuild, jumpTo: jumpTo,
      isAnimating: function () { return animating; },
      getRevealed: function () { return revealed; }
    };
  }

  // =================================================================
  // Section 1
  // =================================================================
  (function () {
    var canvas = $("fern-canvas-1");
    var ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
    var summaryEl = $("fern-s1-summary");
    var x0In = $("fern-s1-x0"), y0In = $("fern-s1-y0");
    var sliders = {
      a: $("fern-s1-a"), b: $("fern-s1-b"), c: $("fern-s1-c"),
      d: $("fern-s1-d"), e: $("fern-s1-e"), f: $("fern-s1-f")
    };
    var vals = {
      a: $("fern-s1-a-val"), b: $("fern-s1-b-val"), c: $("fern-s1-c-val"),
      d: $("fern-s1-d-val"), e: $("fern-s1-e-val"), f: $("fern-s1-f-val")
    };
    var applyBtn = $("fern-s1-apply"), resetBtn = $("fern-s1-reset");
    var count = 0;

    function safe(v, dflt) { var n = parseFloat(v); return isFinite(n) ? n : dflt; }

    function render() {
      var x0 = safe(x0In.value, 1.0), y0 = safe(y0In.value, 1.0);
      var a = safe(sliders.a.value, 0), b = safe(sliders.b.value, 0);
      var c = safe(sliders.c.value, 0), d = safe(sliders.d.value, 0);
      var e = safe(sliders.e.value, 0), f = safe(sliders.f.value, 0);
      for (var k in vals) vals[k].textContent = safe(sliders[k].value, 0).toFixed(2);

      var res = iterateSingleRule(x0, y0, a, b, c, d, e, f, count);
      var xs = res.xs, ys = res.ys;

      var W = canvas.width, H = canvas.height;
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#fbfbf8";
      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
      var b2 = dataBounds(xs, ys, 0, xs.length);
      var xpad = (b2[1] - b2[0]) * 0.15 + 0.4, ypad = (b2[3] - b2[2]) * 0.15 + 0.4;
      var tr = (function () {
        var xmin = b2[0] - xpad, xmax = b2[1] + xpad, ymin = b2[2] - ypad, ymax = b2[3] + ypad;
        var dataW = Math.max(xmax - xmin, 1e-6), dataH = Math.max(ymax - ymin, 1e-6);
        var scale = Math.min(W / dataW, H / dataH);
        var offX = (W - dataW * scale) / 2, offY = (H - dataH * scale) / 2;
        return {
          sx: function (x) { return offX + (x - xmin) * scale; },
          sy: function (y) { return H - (offY + (y - ymin) * scale); }
        };
      })();

      // guide lines through the origin
      ctx.strokeStyle = "#e3e3e3"; ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(0, tr.sy(0)); ctx.lineTo(W, tr.sy(0)); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(tr.sx(0), 0); ctx.lineTo(tr.sx(0), H); ctx.stroke();

      // connecting line
      ctx.strokeStyle = "#9aa0a6"; ctx.globalAlpha = 0.7; ctx.lineWidth = 1.0;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (var i = 0; i < xs.length; i++) {
        var px = tr.sx(xs[i]), py = tr.sy(ys[i]);
        if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(px, py); else ctx.lineTo(px, py);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;

      // intermediate points
      if (xs.length > 2) {
        ctx.fillStyle = "#9aa0a6";
        for (var j = 1; j < xs.length - 1; j++) {
          var qx = tr.sx(xs[j]), qy = tr.sy(ys[j]);
          ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(qx, qy, 3, 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.fill();
        }
      }
      // start point (black) and current point (pink)
      ctx.fillStyle = "#222";
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(tr.sx(xs[0]), tr.sy(ys[0]), 5, 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.fill();
      if (xs.length > 1) {
        ctx.fillStyle = "#d81b60";
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(tr.sx(xs[xs.length - 1]), tr.sy(ys[ys.length - 1]), 5.5, 0, 2 * Math.PI);
        ctx.fill();
      }

      var lines = [];
      if (count === 0) {
        lines.push('Press "Apply this rule again" to map the black point using the rule above -- the new point will appear in pink.');
      } else {
        var px2 = xs[xs.length - 2], py2 = ys[ys.length - 2];
        var nx = xs[xs.length - 1], ny = ys[ys.length - 1];
        lines.push("<strong>After " + count + " application" + (count !== 1 ? "s" : "") + " of the rule:</strong>");
        lines.push(
          "x&prime; = " + a.toFixed(2) + " &times; " + px2.toFixed(3) + " + " + b.toFixed(2) + " &times; " + py2.toFixed(3) +
          " + " + e.toFixed(2) + " = <strong>" + nx.toFixed(3) + "</strong><br>" +
          "y&prime; = " + c.toFixed(2) + " &times; " + px2.toFixed(3) + " + " + d.toFixed(2) + " &times; " + py2.toFixed(3) +
          " + " + f.toFixed(2) + " = <strong>" + ny.toFixed(3) + "</strong>"
        );
        if (res.clipped) {
          lines.push("This rule doesn't contract -- the point is shooting off to huge values (capped here so the plot doesn't break). Try smaller a/b/c/d values, or press reset.");
        } else if (count >= 5) {
          lines.push("Notice the point is settling towards one fixed spot rather than wandering off -- that's what it means for a rule to <strong>contract</strong>. Every rule used below is built to do exactly this.");
        }
      }
      summaryEl.innerHTML = lines.join("<br><br>");
    }

    applyBtn.addEventListener("click", function () { count = Math.min(count + 1, 30); render(); });
    resetBtn.addEventListener("click", function () { count = 0; render(); });
    x0In.addEventListener("input", render);
    y0In.addEventListener("input", render);
    Object.keys(sliders).forEach(function (k) { sliders[k].addEventListener("input", render); });

    render();
  })();

  // =================================================================
  // Section 2 -- Sierpinski triangle
  // =================================================================
  (function () {
    var TRIANGLE_CORNERS = [[0.0, 0.0], [1.0, 0.0], [0.5, 0.866]];
    var TRIANGLE_NAMES = ["Corner A", "Corner B", "Corner C"];
    var TRIANGLE_COLORS = ["#c0392b", "#2e7d32", "#1565c0"];
    var TRIANGLE_RULES = TRIANGLE_CORNERS.map(function (c) {
      return [0.5, 0.0, 0.0, 0.5, c[0] / 2, c[1] / 2, 1.0 / 3.0];
    });
    var MAX_POINTS_2 = 8000, SLOW_POINTS_2 = 18, SLOW_DELAY_2 = 300, FAST_FRAMES_2 = 12, FAST_DELAY_2 = 100;

    var canvas = $("fern-canvas-2");
    var ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
    var nSlider = $("fern-s2-n");
    var animateBtn = $("fern-s2-animate");
    var summaryEl = $("fern-s2-summary");

    function target() { return parseInt(nSlider.value, 10); }

    function onReveal(revealed, animating) {
      var n = Math.max(revealed, 1);
      var res = generatePoints(n, TRIANGLE_RULES, SEED);
      var highlightI = (animating && revealed >= 1) ? revealed - 1 : null;
      drawPoints(ctx, canvas.width, canvas.height, res.xs, res.ys, res.ruleIdx, n, "rule", TRIANGLE_COLORS, null, highlightI);

      var probs = normalizeProbs(TRIANGLE_RULES);
      var lines = [];
      if (animating && revealed >= 1 && revealed <= SLOW_POINTS_2) {
        lines.push(stepFormulaHtml(revealed, target(), TRIANGLE_RULES, res.ruleIdx, res.xs, res.ys, TRIANGLE_NAMES, probs));
      } else if (animating) {
        lines.push("<strong>Building the triangle: " + fmtN(revealed) + " / " + fmtN(target()) + " points</strong>");
      } else {
        lines.push("<strong>Points plotted:</strong> " + fmtN(revealed));
      }
      summaryEl.innerHTML = lines.join("<br><br>");
    }

    var builder = makeWatchBuilder({
      slowPoints: SLOW_POINTS_2, slowDelay: SLOW_DELAY_2,
      fastFrames: FAST_FRAMES_2, fastDelay: FAST_DELAY_2,
      onReveal: onReveal, targetFn: target
    });

    nSlider.addEventListener("input", function () { builder.fastRebuild(1500); });
    animateBtn.addEventListener("click", function () { builder.start(); });

    builder.fastRebuild(1500);
  })();

  // =================================================================
  // Section 3 -- Barnsley's fern, simplified
  // =================================================================
  (function () {
    var CLASSIC_RULES = [
      [0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.16, 0.00, 0.00, 0.01],
      [0.85, 0.04, -0.04, 0.85, 0.00, 1.60, 0.85],
      [0.20, -0.26, 0.23, 0.22, 0.00, 1.60, 0.07],
      [-0.15, 0.28, 0.26, 0.24, 0.00, 0.44, 0.07]
    ];
    var RULE_NAMES = ["Stem", "Whole-fern copy", "Left leaflet", "Right leaflet"];
    var RULE_COLORS = ["#6b4226", "#2e7d32", "#1565c0", "#c77f00"];
    var SLOW_POINTS = 24, SLOW_DELAY = 300, FAST_FRAMES = 14, FAST_DELAY = 100;

    var canvas = $("fern-canvas");
    var ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
    var nSlider = $("fern-s3-n");
    var animateBtn = $("fern-s3-animate");
    var resetBtn = $("fern-s3-reset");
    var summaryEl = $("fern-s3-summary");
    var rulesListEl = $("fern-s3-rules-list");
    var rotationSlider = $("fern-s3-rotation"), leafletSlider = $("fern-s3-leaflet");
    var stemSlider = $("fern-s3-stem"), leanSlider = $("fern-s3-lean");
    var rotationVal = $("fern-s3-rotation-val"), leafletVal = $("fern-s3-leaflet-val");
    var stemVal = $("fern-s3-stem-val"), leanVal = $("fern-s3-lean-val");
    var colorRadios = root.querySelectorAll('input[name="fern-s3-color"]');

    function colorMode() {
      var checked = root.querySelector('input[name="fern-s3-color"]:checked');
      return checked ? checked.value : "natural";
    }

    function simplifiedRules(rotationDeg, leafletScale, stemMult, lean) {
      var rules = CLASSIC_RULES.map(function (r) { return r.slice(); });
      rules[0][3] = CLASSIC_RULES[0][3] * stemMult;
      rules[1][1] = CLASSIC_RULES[1][1] + lean;
      var theta = rotationDeg * Math.PI / 180;
      var ct = Math.cos(theta), st = Math.sin(theta);
      [2, 3].forEach(function (i) {
        var a = CLASSIC_RULES[i][0], b = CLASSIC_RULES[i][1], c = CLASSIC_RULES[i][2], d = CLASSIC_RULES[i][3];
        rules[i][0] = (ct * a - st * c) * leafletScale;
        rules[i][1] = (ct * b - st * d) * leafletScale;
        rules[i][2] = (st * a + ct * c) * leafletScale;
        rules[i][3] = (st * b + ct * d) * leafletScale;
      });
      return rules;
    }

    function currentRules() {
      return simplifiedRules(
        parseFloat(rotationSlider.value), parseFloat(leafletSlider.value),
        parseFloat(stemSlider.value), parseFloat(leanSlider.value)
      );
    }

    function target() { return parseInt(nSlider.value, 10); }

    function updateSliderLabels() {
      rotationVal.textContent = parseFloat(rotationSlider.value).toFixed(0);
      leafletVal.textContent = parseFloat(leafletSlider.value).toFixed(1);
      stemVal.textContent = parseFloat(stemSlider.value).toFixed(1);
      leanVal.textContent = parseFloat(leanSlider.value).toFixed(1);
    }

    function updateRulesTable(rules, probs) {
      var html = "";
      for (var i = 0; i < RULE_NAMES.length; i++) {
        var r = rules[i];
        html += "<li><strong>" + RULE_NAMES[i] + "</strong>: a=" + r[0].toFixed(3) + ", b=" + r[1].toFixed(3) +
          ", c=" + r[2].toFixed(3) + ", d=" + r[3].toFixed(3) + ", e=" + r[4].toFixed(3) + ", f=" + r[5].toFixed(3) +
          ", p=" + Math.round(probs[i] * 100) + "%</li>";
      }
      rulesListEl.innerHTML = html;
    }

    function onReveal(revealed, animating) {
      updateSliderLabels();
      var n = Math.max(revealed, 1);
      var rules = currentRules();
      var res = generatePoints(n, rules, SEED);
      var highlightI = (animating && revealed >= 1) ? revealed - 1 : null;
      drawPoints(ctx, canvas.width, canvas.height, res.xs, res.ys, res.ruleIdx, n, colorMode(), RULE_COLORS, "#2f7a3d", highlightI);

      var probs = normalizeProbs(rules);
      var lines = [];
      if (animating && revealed >= 1 && revealed <= SLOW_POINTS) {
        lines.push(stepFormulaHtml(revealed, target(), rules, res.ruleIdx, res.xs, res.ys, RULE_NAMES, probs));
      } else if (animating) {
        lines.push("<strong>Building the fern: " + fmtN(revealed) + " / " + fmtN(target()) + " points</strong>");
      } else {
        lines.push("<strong>Points plotted:</strong> " + fmtN(revealed));
      }

      if (res.clipped) {
        lines.push("<strong>These settings don't contract</strong> -- points are shooting off to huge values and being capped so the app doesn't crash. Try a smaller leaflet size or a smaller lean, or press \"Reset to Barnsley's fern\".");
      }

      var ruleLines = RULE_NAMES.map(function (name, i) {
        return "&bull; <strong>" + name + "</strong>: " + Math.round(probs[i] * 100) + "%";
      }).join("<br>");
      lines.push("Every point is drawn by picking one of 4 rules at random, each with a fixed probability, then plotting where it sends the previous point:<br>" + ruleLines);
      lines.push("On Barnsley's own numbers, the <strong>whole-fern copy</strong> rule alone (picked 85% of the time) draws a complete smaller copy of the entire fern -- the same self-similarity idea from step 2, just with cleverer rules.");
      if (colorMode() === "rule") {
        lines.push("Colours above show which rule drew each point.");
      }

      summaryEl.innerHTML = lines.join("<br><br>");
      updateRulesTable(rules, probs);
    }

    var builder = makeWatchBuilder({
      slowPoints: SLOW_POINTS, slowDelay: SLOW_DELAY,
      fastFrames: FAST_FRAMES, fastDelay: FAST_DELAY,
      onReveal: onReveal, targetFn: target
    });

    nSlider.addEventListener("input", function () { builder.fastRebuild(3000); });
    animateBtn.addEventListener("click", function () { builder.start(); });
    [rotationSlider, leafletSlider, stemSlider, leanSlider].forEach(function (s) {
      s.addEventListener("input", function () { builder.fastRebuild(3000); });
    });
    colorRadios.forEach(function (r) {
      r.addEventListener("change", function () { onReveal(builder.getRevealed(), builder.isAnimating()); });
    });
    resetBtn.addEventListener("click", function () {
      rotationSlider.value = 0; leafletSlider.value = 1.0; stemSlider.value = 1.0; leanSlider.value = 0.0;
      builder.fastRebuild(3000);
    });

    builder.fastRebuild(3000);
  })();

})();
</script>
```

:::

Turn on "By generating rule" to see the self-similarity directly: colour each point by which of the four rules drew it, and the largest green portion -- on its own -- already looks like a complete, smaller fern. That is exactly what it means to break a structure down into smaller parts that are the same shape as the whole.

:::
